>> {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":3,"method":"session/prompt","params":{"prompt":[{"text":"\u003cinstructions\u003e\nGlitched runs you in a thread. Its MCP server glitched gives you the tool delegate_task, which starts a child agent in a thread of its own, under this one.\n\n- Follow the user's delegation preferences and the repository's instructions. That the tool is there does not by itself call for delegating work.\n- The child starts at once, with this thread's folder, permissions and model unless you pick another model. It does not see this conversation, so give it a self-contained brief.\n- Each time a child's turn ends done or failed, its report reaches this thread as a new message, in your next turn. Do not wait or poll for it: carry on, or end your turn.\n- A child that delegates in turn reports each turn it ends done or failed, so it can report before its own children finish and again after. Its latest report is the current one. If you delegate and end your turn while children still work, say so in your reply: that reply is your report to your parent.\n- The user sees each child and can open it. A child cannot get wider permissions than this thread.\n- Use a new client_request_id for each new task, and the same one to retry a call, so a retry does not start a second child.\n\u003c/instructions\u003e\n\nsay hi and list the files here","type":"text"}],"sessionId":"fd193820-87da-4415-b480-f39c57a6cfff"}}
<< {"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"fd193820-87da-4415-b480-f39c57a6cfff","update":{"sessionUpdate":"available_commands_update","availableCommands":[{"name":"goal","description":"Run until the specified goal is completely finished."},{"name":"compact","description":"Compact the conversation now (summarize history to free up the context window)."},{"name":"schedule","description":"Run an instruction on a recurring schedule or as a one-time timer."},{"name":"browser","description":"Invoke a browser agent for web tasks."},{"name":"plan","description":"Plan carefully before executing a task."},{"name":"grill-me","description":"Interview me to align on a plan."},{"name":"learn","description":"Reflect on recent successes or corrections to capture reusable skills or rules."},{"name":"agy-customizations","description":"Comprehensive guide and reference for the Antigravity Customization System. Use to explain how customizations work, their loading priority, discovery mechanisms, and to guide the creation of skills, rules, plugins, hooks, and MCP servers."},{"name":"antigravity-guide","description":"Provides a comprehensive guide, quick reference, and sitemap for Google Antigravity (AGY), including the Antigravity CLI (agy), Antigravity 2.0, Antigravity IDE, Python SDK, slash commands, keybindings, and customizations (skills, rules, MCP, sidecars). Activate this skill when the user asks questions about how to use, configure, or customize Antigravity, AGY, the agy CLI, the Antigravity IDE, or Antigravity 2.0."},{"name":"run-workflow","description":"How to write and run a dynamic workflow script with the `run_workflow` tool: a Python script that orchestrates many agents with `agent`, `parallel`, `pipeline`, and `phase`. Use when a task splits into many independent or staged pieces of agent work (fan out over files, modules, bugs, or review angles, then aggregate), or when the user asks for a workflow. Don't use for a single delegated task (use a subagent) or for legacy workflow files (see migrate-workflows)."},{"name":"swarm","description":"(Preview \u0026 Quota Heavy) Run a swarm: several agents working in parallel on one task, each in its own conversation, collaborating through a shared message board. Use when the work splits into pieces that can be done at the same time, or when a second pair of eyes should check the first pair's work."}]}}}
